# Start Loan Journey (ADR-018 — Product Architecture Approved)

**Status:** ACCEPTED · supersedes prior Contact → Opportunity Workspace shortcut  
**ADR:** `docs/adr/ADR-018-start-loan-journey-draft-lead-information.md`

## Canonical flow

```
Contact
  → Start Loan Journey
  → Draft Opportunity (identity only — no fabricated business values)
  → Loan Journey (Execution Hub) — orchestration, NOT Deal workspace
  → Lead Information Workspace — Opportunity Registry capture only
  → Save Product + Required Amount → Requirement Captured
  → Opportunity Workspace (execution / enrichment)
  → Documents → Credit → LIFE → Pipeline
```

## Lifecycle

`Draft` → `Requirement Captured` → `Active Opportunity`

## Hard rules

1. Start creates **Draft** Opportunity — identity only. No fabricated product/amount/lending/transaction.
2. **Requirement Captured** only when **Product** and **Required Amount** are saved on Opportunity Registry.
3. Execution Hub = journey orchestration at **`/loan-journey`** (Wave 3). Never mint Deal/LoanFile on this entry path. Do **not** rename `/loan-files` Deal workspace in Wave 3 — preserve backward compatibility.
4. Lead Information Workspace writes **only** to Opportunity Registry — never LoanFile/Deal models; never `LoanCreateFormDialog`.
5. Opportunity Workspace begins **only after** Requirement Captured — not for initial requirement capture.
6. Lending type stays **Not Specified** until captured or Policy/approved derivation.
7. Align with **CAD-2026-001** — no compatibility-layer business invent.

## Implementation

Future work must follow ADR-018 waves. Do not restore Contact → `/credit-bench` as Start landing.  
Wave 3 Hub route lock: `.cursor/rules/loan-journey-execution-hub-route.mdc` · `docs/co-arch-003/CO-ARCH-ADR-018-WAVE3-HUB-ROUTE-LOCK.md`
